module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Geometrically.Irreducible
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.QuasiCompact

/-! # Spreading geometric irreducibility from the generic fibre

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0559.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u
open CategoryTheory Topology
namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A finite type morphism with geometrically irreducible generic fibre has
geometrically irreducible fibres near the generic point.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0559, lemma-geometrically-irreducible-generic-fibre.
Proof: replace the irreducible base by its reduction. Reduction is a universal
homeomorphism and does not change geometric fibre irreducibility. Reduce the source
and use generic flatness in its finite-presentation form (Proposition 29.28.1) to
shrink to a flat finitely presented morphism. Choose a nonempty affine open of the
source. Its generic fibre is dense; Tag 054X makes it dense in all geometric fibres
after shrinking. A finite purely inseparable extension of the function field makes
the reduced source function field separably generated. Spread this extension by
scaling field generators: if b^q = a/d, then (db)^q = a*d^(q-1) is integral over the
base. The finite algebra generated by these scaled elements is radicial, so its
spectrum is a universal homeomorphism and preserves the geometric fibre tests.
Reduce again and restore flatness and finite presentation by Proposition 29.28.1.
A separating transcendence basis gives a birational absolutely irreducible
hypersurface; clear denominators to spread the common affine open and apply Tag
054X again. Tag 0557 makes the hypersurface fibres geometrically irreducible on a
nonempty base open: make its equation monic by substitutions of separated powers,
form finite type coefficient algebras for the finitely many possible positive monic
factor degrees, and use Nullstellensatz at the generic fibre to kill each algebra
by inverting one nonzero base element. Their product rules out all factorizations
in every field specialization. Density transfers irreducibility to the original
fibres. Shrink to the open image of the flat finitely presented morphism for
nonemptiness. Descend the open through the universal homeomorphisms; its nonemptiness
means it contains the generic point.

(blueprint: lem-sbc-generic-geometric-irreducibility-shrink) -/
theorem exists_open_generic_geometric_irreducibility_shrink {X T : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ T) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] [QuasiCompact f]
    (η : T) (hη : IsGenericPoint η Set.univ)
    (hgeom : GeometricallyIrreducible (f.fiberToSpecResidueField η)) :
    ∃ U : T.Opens, η ∈ U ∧ ∀ t, t ∈ U →
      GeometricallyIrreducible (f.fiberToSpecResidueField t) := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
